  "id": "Hackney-2025_0409",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed works, including the removal of internal walls, floors, and ceilings and the boxing-in of decorative ground-floor columns, have resulted in the unjustified loss of significant historic fabric and harm to the architectural and historic interest of the Grade II listed building. The proposal fails to preserve the special interest of the listed building and does not demonstrate public benefits sufficient to outweigh the identified harm. The development is therefore contrary to Sections 16 and 66 of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Paragraph 215 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy HC1 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies LP1 and LP3 of the Hackney Local Plan (2020).&lt;/p&gt;"
